export const termsEn = "# Terms of Use\n\nEffective: [EFFECTIVE DATE]\n\nThese Terms of Use (\"Terms\") govern your use of the Nuni and Fourpop apps (each an \"App\") published by Chagyung (\"we\", \"us\"). By downloading or using an App you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.\n\n## 1. The Apps\n\nNuni is a mood diary. Fourpop is a photo booth app. Both run on your device and store your content on your device (and, if you turn it on, in your own iCloud). We do not operate accounts and you do not need to sign up.\n\n## 2. Who may use the Apps\n\nYou must be at least 13 years old, or the minimum age required in your country to use an App without parental consent. If you are under 18, your parent or guardian must agree to these Terms.\n\n## 3. Your content\n\nEverything you create in an App — diary entries, tags, notes, photos, photo strips — is yours. We do not receive, see or store it. You are responsible for your content and for backing it up (Settings › Backup / Export). Deleting the App deletes the content on that device.\n\n## 4. Paid features\n\n- Each App offers an auto-renewing subscription (\"Premium\"). Fourpop also offers one-time purchases (frame and sticker packs). Prices are shown in the App in your local currency before you buy.\n- Payment is charged to your Apple ID at confirmation of purchase. A subscription renews automatically at the same price and period unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. You can manage or cancel it in your App Store account settings. A free trial, where offered, converts to a paid subscription unless cancelled before the trial ends.\n- Refunds are handled by Apple under App Store terms. We cannot issue refunds directly.\n- One-time purchases stay yours after a subscription ends. Seasonal packs may be withdrawn from sale on the date shown, but packs you bought remain usable.\n\n## 5. Acceptable use\n\nDo not use an App to create or share content that is unlawful, infringes someone's rights, or harms others. Do not reverse engineer, copy or resell the App or its frames, stickers and illustrations. Our frames, stickers, illustrations and the Nuni mascot are our copyrighted works; you may use them inside your own photo strips and share those freely, including commercially, but you may not redistribute the assets themselves.\n\n## 6. Third-party services\n\nThe Apps use Apple (App Store, iCloud, StoreKit), RevenueCat (purchase validation) and Google Firebase (crash reports and anonymous usage analytics). Their terms apply to those services. Sharing to Instagram, TikTok or other apps is governed by those apps.\n\n## 7. Changes to the Apps and these Terms\n\nWe may add, change or remove features, and may update these Terms. Material changes are shown in the App before they take effect. Continued use after that means you accept the new Terms.\n\n## 8. Disclaimer and liability\n\nThe Apps are provided \"as is\". Nuni is a personal diary and not a medical or mental-health service; it does not diagnose or treat anything. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for loss of data, lost profits or indirect damages, and our total liability to you is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these Terms limits rights you have under consumer protection law in Vietnam, Thailand or your country of residence.\n\n## 9. Termination\n\nYou may stop using an App at any time by deleting it. We may suspend an App's paid services if you breach these Terms.\n\n## 10. Governing law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea, without prejudice to mandatory consumer protections in your country of residence. Disputes will be resolved in the courts of Seoul, Korea, unless local law gives you the right to sue where you live.\n\n## 11. Contact\n\nChagyung · nunicozy@gmail.com · Seoul, Republic of Korea (individual developer)\n\nApple's standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement also applies to your use of the Apps: https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\n";

export const privacyEn = "# Privacy Policy\n\nEffective: [EFFECTIVE DATE]\n\nThis policy explains what Nuni and Fourpop (each an \"App\"), published by Chagyung (\"we\"), do with information. The short version: your diary and photos stay on your device; we only receive anonymous usage statistics, crash reports and purchase records.\n\n## 1. What stays on your device\n\n- **Nuni**: mood entries, tags, notes, photos, streaks, settings.\n- **Fourpop**: captured photos, finished photo strips, downloaded frame and sticker packs, settings.\n\nThis content is stored only on your device. If you turn on iCloud backup (Nuni), it is copied to your own iCloud account under Apple's privacy terms. We never receive it and cannot read it.\n\n## 2. What we collect\n\n| Data | Purpose | Service | Linked to you? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| App usage events (screens opened, features used, such as \"entry created\" or \"strip shared\"), device model, iOS version, app version, language, country | Understand which features are used and fix problems | Google Firebase Analytics | No. An anonymous installation ID only |\n| Crash reports (stack trace, device state at crash) | Fix crashes | Google Firebase Crashlytics | No |\n| Purchase records (product bought, date, anonymous app user ID, Apple receipt) | Unlock what you paid for, restore purchases, prevent fraud | RevenueCat, Apple | No. Apple knows your identity; we and RevenueCat see only an anonymous ID |\n| Frame and sticker pack downloads (which pack, when, IP address in server logs) | Deliver content | Cloudflare | No |\n\nWe do not collect your name, email, phone number, contacts, precise location, or the content of your diary or photos. Analytics events never contain diary text, tag names you typed, or images.\n\n## 3. Why we are allowed to process this (legal basis)\n\nWe process usage and crash data to run and improve the Apps (legitimate interest), and purchase records to perform the contract with you. Where your country's law requires consent for analytics, we ask for it on first launch and you can withdraw it in Settings › Privacy at any time.\n\n## 4. Who receives data\n\nApple (App Store, iCloud, StoreKit), Google (Firebase), RevenueCat and Cloudflare act as our processors and only use data to provide their services. Data may be stored on servers outside Vietnam and Thailand (United States, EU). We rely on these providers' standard data protection terms for such transfers. We do not sell data and do not use it for advertising.\n\n## 5. How long we keep data\n\nUsage events and crash reports: up to 14 months, then deleted or aggregated. Purchase records: as long as needed to honour your purchases and for the legal retention period for financial records.\n\n## 6. Your rights\n\nDepending on where you live (including under Vietnam's Decree 13/2023 on personal data protection and Thailand's Personal Data Protection Act), you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to processing of your personal data, to data portability, and to withdraw consent. Because the data we hold is anonymous, we usually cannot identify which records are yours; if you send us your anonymous installation ID (Settings › Privacy › Copy ID) we will delete the related analytics and crash data within 30 days. You can delete everything on your device from Settings › Delete all data, and export your Nuni entries from Settings › Export.\n\n## 7. Children\n\nThe Apps are not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. Parents who believe a child has used an App can contact us.\n\n## 8. Security\n\nContent on your device is protected by iOS device encryption; Nuni offers an additional Face ID / passcode lock. Data sent to our providers is encrypted in transit (TLS).\n\n## 9. Changes\n\nWe will show material changes in the App before they take effect and update the date above.\n\n## 10. Contact\n\nData controller: Chagyung, Seoul, Republic of Korea (individual developer) · nunicozy@gmail.com\n";

